Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; KVFX Tools - enable Adobe CEP debug mode
;
; After Effects refuses to load an UNSIGNED extension unless PlayerDebugMode is
; set. KVFX Tools is not code-signed yet (that is a Phase 14 deliverable), so
; this is required to run it.
;
; What this changes:
;   - Writes one value per CEP version under HKEY_CURRENT_USER.
;   - HKCU means your user account only. No administrator rights are needed and
;     no other user on this machine is affected.
;   - It only relaxes the signature requirement for Adobe extension loading. It
;     changes nothing else about Windows or After Effects.
;
; It is fully reversible: run disable-cep-debug.reg to undo it.
;
; CSXS.12 covers After Effects 26.x, CSXS.11 covers 22.x-25.x. Setting the one
; you do not have installed is harmless. For a future CEP version, copy a block
; below and change the number.
;
; Quit and reopen After Effects after running this.

[HKEY_CURRENT_USER\Software\Adobe\CSXS.12]
"PlayerDebugMode"="1"

[HKEY_CURRENT_USER\Software\Adobe\CSXS.11]
"PlayerDebugMode"="1"
